   "text": "This SMILES was read region by region from the drawing. It describes a spiro-oxindole MDM2-type ligand joined through a benzamide and a four-carbon linker to a lenalidomide-type cereblon ligand.\n\n- **Cereblon end:** A 4-amino isoindolin-1-one carries a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group on the ring nitrogen. The amine NH is on the aromatic carbon next to the carbon bearing the CH2. It connects to a chain of four CH2 groups, which ends at an amide NH.\n- **Linker:** The chain runs from the amide NH through the four CH2 groups to the isoindolinone NH. The amide C=O is on a para-substituted benzene ring. The ring's other substituent is an NH that forms a second amide with the pyrrolidine carboxyl.\n- **Pyrrolidine core:** The ring contains the CH bearing the carboxamide, an NH, a spiro carbon shared with a cyclohexane, a second spiro carbon shared with the oxindole, and a CH bearing the 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl group.\n- **Oxindole:** The spiro carbon is attached to the aryl ring and the lactam C=O, and the aryl ring carries Cl at C6.\n- **Stereochemistry:** Wedges and hashes are drawn on three carbons.\n  - The carboxamide CH is R.\n  - The aryl-bearing CH is S.\n  - The oxindole spiro carbon is R.\n  - The cyclohexane spiro carbon is not a stereocentre, because its two ring CH2 arms are identical.\n\nI assigned the three centres by CIP priorities and then set the @/@@ marks to match, but I did not check the result with software.\n\nSMILES: O=C(Nc1ccc(cc1)C(=O)NCCCCNc1cccc2c1CN(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)[C@@H]1NC2(CCCCC2)[C@@]3(C(=O)Nc4cc(Cl)ccc34)[C@H]1c1cccc(Cl)c1F"
